    <exercise number="">
        <title>Question 4.B</title>
        <statement>
            <p>Is it possible for a matrix to have a zero for an eigenvalue? What does it mean if zero is an eigenvalue for a matrix?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution>
            <p>It is possible for a matrix to have an eigenvalue that is zero and when this happens it forces the matrix to be singular.</p>
        </solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise number="">
        <title>Question 4.C</title>
